{
  "version": "0.3",
  "_readme": "Allowlist for scripts/petri_audit/sanitizer.py: the projection of a raw Inspect .eval log that may enter the public repository (docs/petri_integration_design.md section 9). Anything not named here is removed and counted in the manifest's redaction report. The raw log is never committed; it is bound to the manifest by sha256 and held under the custody the manifest records. Keys listed under forbidden_keys are handled in two ways. Inside the values the projection keeps whole because the model provider fills them (a model event's output apart from its choices' messages, which are projected; every value a projected message keeps; a tool event's arguments and internal), a forbidden key at any depth is dropped and counted in the redaction report's forbidden_keys_dropped, by path with list indices elided. Anywhere else a forbidden key refuses the whole output, allowlist or not, as a second line of defence. Data, not code: a change here is a new sanitiser allowlist version and a new allowlist digest in every manifest that used it.",
  "_version_0_3": "Version 0.3 changes only this readme, which now describes the drop-and-count rule above. Keys, event types and forbidden keys are unchanged from 0.2. Under 0.2 a forbidden key inside a provider-filled value refused the output. That is how w2e3 (run 35937014168, 2026-09-24 00:09 UTC) failed at Adapt: every Anthropic response carried a top-level diagnostics field that anthropic 0.105.0's non-beta Message type does not declare, and inspect_ai 0.3.237 records undeclared response fields as output.metadata.extra_body. Any log that 0.2 accepted projects to the same content under 0.3.",
